TypeScript Lesson 13: Generics <T> 🚀
Aaj hum Generics seekhenge. Ye TypeScript ka important concept hai, jo professional code aur real projects mein kaafi use hota hai.
Simple words mein: Generics se hum ek hi function ko different data types ke saath reuse kar sakte hain, bina type safety lose kiye.
1. Generics ki zaroorat kyun hai?
Maan lo tumhe ek function banana hai jo input ko return kare.
Normal number function:
function getNumber(value: number): number {
    return value;
}

console.log(getNumber(100));


Lekin agar string bhi return karni ho, to alag function banana padega:
function getString(value: string): string {
    return value;
}


Kya hum ek hi function se dono kaam kar sakte hain? Haan, Generics se!
2. Pehla Generic function
function getValue<T>(value: T): T {
    return value;
}

console.log(getValue<number>(100));
console.log(getValue<string>("Hello"));
console.log(getValue<boolean>(true));


Output:
100
Hello
true


Code ko samjho:
- T ek placeholder hai, jo type represent karta hai.
- <T> batata hai ki function generic hai.
- value: T ka matlab input ka type T hai.
- : T ka matlab return value ka type bhi T hai.
Agar T = number hai, to function number leta aur number return karta hai.
Agar T = string hai, to function string leta aur string return karta hai.
Memory trick: T ko temporary Type samjho. T koi special fixed type nahi, sirf ek conventional naam hai.
3. TypeScript khud type infer bhi kar sakta hai
Har baar <number> ya <string> likhna zaroori nahi.
function getValue<T>(value: T): T {
    return value;
}

let result1 = getValue(500);
let result2 = getValue("TypeScript");

console.log(result1);
console.log(result2);


TypeScript automatically samajh leta hai:
- getValue(500) → T is number
- getValue("TypeScript") → T is string
4. Generic function with arrays
Maan lo humein array ka first item nikalna hai. Array numbers ka ho sakta hai ya strings ka.
function getFirst<T>(items: T[]): T | undefined {
    return items[0];
}

console.log(getFirst<number>([10, 20, 30]));
console.log(getFirst<string>(["Apple", "Mango"]));
console.log(getFirst<boolean>([true, false]));


Output:
10
Apple
true


T[] ka matlab hai T type ke items ki array.
T | undefined isliye likha hai kyunki empty array mein first item nahi hoga.
console.log(getFirst<number>([])); // undefined


5. Multiple generic types
Ek function mein multiple generic types bhi ho sakte hain.
function pair<T, U>(first: T, second: U): [T, U] {
    return [first, second];
}

console.log(pair<string, number>("Age", 25));
console.log(pair<boolean, string>(true, "Active"));


Output:
["Age", 25]
[true, "Active"]


Yahan:
- T first value ka type hai.
- U second value ka type hai.
- [T, U] ek tuple type hai, jisme pehli aur doosri value ke types defined hain.

